    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver: the $4.50 cancellation fee is refunded in full to the rider, and no driver compensation is payable.\n\nWhat the record shows. The driver accepted the trip at 22:30:19, drove to the pickup, and tapped 'I'm Here' at 22:38:37 while stationary 0.31 m from the pin. EV-GPS-02717 places 19 consecutive accuracy-qualifying fixes inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius, so the arrival test in POL-NS-02 is met and the marker is genuine; POL-NS-05 does not fire and the waiting clock is not recomputed. The driver's account is broadly borne out by the event chain — he was en route about 8.3 minutes and waited about three minutes — so the rider's description of an 'almost immediate' cancellation is not supported by the telemetry. That does not, however, decide the fee.\n\nWhy the fee cannot stand. POL-NS-01(c) requires a continuous in-geofence dwell of at least the free waiting period in force, which for this trip is 180 seconds (trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec, the figure POL-NS-01(c) directs be read from the record). The platform's own trace measures the driver's single in-geofence run at 179 seconds, from the first qualifying fix at 22:38:37 to termination at 22:41:36; 180 seconds from 22:38:37 elapsed at 22:41:37, so the trip was terminated one second early. Limb (c) fails on the dwell and limb (d) fails on the timing, and under POL-NS-06 the fee is not chargeable and is refunded in full, whether or not the rider was present. The shortfall cannot be bridged: POL-NS-06(i) permits separate in-geofence intervals to be summed only where a present and populated traffic advisory of a qualifying type covers the pickup road, and EV-ADVIS-02717-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT); in any event the trace shows only one in-geofence interval (run_count 1). POL-NS-06 is strict liability — the waiting period is the consideration the fee purchases — so the driver's submission that the one-second gap is a boundary effect of a 10-second export cadence does not displace the measured figure.\n\nDriver compensation. POL-NS-07 pays 80 percent of the fee only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full and no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces it. Here POL-NS-01 fails and POL-NS-06 displaces the charge, so no payout arises. The anti-farming check is not reached; had it been, the driver's profile (no_show_terminations_30d 2, completed_trips_30d 91, rate 0.022) would not have tripped it, and no other profile field bears on the case. The rider's own POL-NS-04 submission — that the rider sent nothing and her track sat 895–903 m from the pin — is accepted but moot, since POL-NS-04 is not needed to reach this outcome.\n\nAmount, evidence and execution. The refunded figure is the cancellation-fee line on the ledger: EV-FARE-02717 shows cancellation_fee 4.50, total_charged 4.50, payment_status CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd 0.00. The full contested amount of $4.50 is returned. The artifacts carrying the deciding facts, EV-GPS-02717 and EV-TRIP-02717, are both COMPLETE at weight 1.0 with no issue codes, and the fee line reconciles with platform_policy, so POL-NS-08(d) has nothing to bite on, nothing caps confidence below the 0.70 floor and no POL-NS-09 escalation trigger is presented. No clause requires a referral. The monetary effect ($4.50) is below the POL-GEN-05 execution threshold ($8.00), so this ruling is executed automatically."
