    "explanation": "Both parties: this case is decided by the driver's own GPS export and trip record, and they agree with each other. The driver genuinely arrived and his arrival marker was honest: EV-GPS-02717 shows 19 consecutive accuracy-qualifying fixes inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius, the closest 0.31 m from the pin, so POL-NS-01 limb (b) is satisfied and POL-NS-05 does not fire (at the 22:38:37 'I'm Here' tap he was stationary essentially on the pin, far inside both the 50 m radius and the 300 m false-marker leash). The charge nevertheless fails on the waiting clock. POL-NS-01(c) requires the driver to hold position inside the geofence for a continuous dwell of at least the free waiting period in force, which is 180 seconds read from trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec (EV-TRIP-02717). That dwell runs from the first qualifying in-geofence fix at 22:38:37, not from the arrival tap and not from the wait-timer event. EV-GPS-02717 measures the run at 179.0 seconds (derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.duration_sec), a shortfall of 1.0 second. The driver terminated the trip at 22:41:36, one second before the required dwell elapsed at 22:41:37, so limb (d)'s timing requirement also fails: it is true, as the driver says, that RIDER_NO_SHOW is one of the three reason codes limb (d) recognises and that no boarding event is recorded, but limb (d) additionally requires termination at or after the moment the required dwell elapsed, and it was not. The driver's 'boundary effect' argument is rejected: no clause gives a de minimis tolerance on the waiting period, and POL-NS-06 is deliberately strict, so the 1-second shortfall on his own admissible trace is decisive. Bridging under POL-NS-06(i) is unavailable in any event, because run_count is 1 (there is no second in-geofence interval to sum) and EV-ADVIS-02717-01 is MISSING at weight_multiplier 0.0 with issue MISSING_ARTIFACT, which makes limb (i) unavailable rather than exculpatory. The rider's account that the driver 'cancelled almost immediately' is contradicted by the telemetry (accepted 22:30:19, 8.3 minutes en route, cancellation 22:41:36), and the rider sent no message during the waiting window so POL-NS-04 cannot exonerate the rider; neither point changes the outcome, because POL-NS-06 refunds the fee whether or not the rider was present or responsive. On the money: the fare_breakdown line is the cancellation fee of SGD 4.50 with total_charged SGD 4.50, payment_status CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd SGD 0.00 (EV-FARE-02717), and it reconciles exactly to the SGD 4.50 in force, so POL-NS-08(d) has nothing to bite on and there is no integrity defect. The deciding facts are carried by EV-GPS-02717 and EV-TRIP-02717, both COMPLETE at weight_multiplier 1.0 with no issue codes (100% coverage, 10-second cadence, 0.0 s maximum gap), so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is 1.0 and no POL-NS-09 trigger fires. POL-NS-07 pays the driver nothing here, because it pays only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full and no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces it, and POL-NS-06 displaces it; the anti-farming check would not have barred a payout (no_show_terminations_30d 2 is below 4, and 2/91 = 0.022 is below 0.08), but that is moot. Result: the SGD 4.50 cancellation fee is refunded in full to the rider under POL-NS-06 with no driver compensation; the monetary effect (SGD 4.50) is below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold, so it executes automatically. Both parties may appeal once within 30 days under POL-GEN-04."
